  "summary": "Challenge the amended ordinary-text autocomplete adoption plan with three Opus reviewers and a Codex review, then apply the third and final design pass. Four second-pass cuts were reversed: atomic callback refusal returns as (tx) => false | undefined, one private owner per Editable holds a single occurrence and takes keys before Plate shortcuts, composition reads Plite view.isComposing with a DOM preview and a Plite settle operation before explicit activation, and the Plite change is no longer conditional. Occurrences become range anchors opened only by a locally typed trigger. Migration uses first-party default triggers with semantic selection mapping, and cost proof moves to a Benchmark key-to-paint comparison. The plan is challenged and ready for Build; no product code changed.",
